{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c57b","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0aeea-0371-7222-a2de-305ea9e57fab"},"sequence":280,"recorded_at":1780531400000555,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"7588bb01-2c7e-40b5-9895-e75b02229259","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"7588bb01-2c7e-40b5-9895-e75b02229259","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"7588bb01-2c7e-40b5-9895-e75b02229259"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0aeea-85e2-79b3-be66-f76b24089097"},"task_id":"01a0aeea-85e2-79b3-be66-f76b24089097","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0aeea-85e2-79b3-be66-f76b24089097","chunk":"Read text file `/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.task-board/.resources/TASK-260830-17ootk/TASK-260830-17ootk_review-verdict-rev1.md`.\n1|# Review verdict — TASK-260830-17ootk rev1 (CR-TASK-260830-17ootk-1): ACCEPT\n2|\n3|Reviewer run: RUN-260917-be21ad. Method: isolated immutable probes only;\n4|the live Story worktree, index, branch, and HEAD were never mutated by this\n5|review. All product evidence below was reproduced by the reviewer in the\n6|live tree or in an isolated candidate copy (`/tmp/iso17`, since removed),\n7|never accepted from producer logs alone.\n8|\n9|Change Request: `CR-TASK-260830-17ootk-1` rev1, candidate tree\n10|`25b762c5e4dbd97a49d0ef687c082d5941060781` over trunk base\n11|`e4e3e8834675cf3814effd3b2673b4931dfbf311`.\n12|Normative authority: pinned `internal/specdoc/SPEC.v0.6.0.md` §§5.4,\n13|10.5–10.6, 13.12–13.13.\n14|\n15|## Verdict: ACCEPT (route to `integrating` via `accept_cr`, evidence = this file)\n16|\n17|## 1. Whole-Story diff — PASS\n18|\n19|- `git verify-commit bde093e` and `8a757e0`: Good signatures (oparin@me.com).\n20|- `git diff --name-only e4e3e88..25b762c` = 38 paths: the 27 committed\n21|  checkpoint paths (sessckpt/matjournal/traceability/README/LOGBOOK) plus\n22|  this leaf's 11 `internal/crashgate/` files and 6 leaf-modified files.\n23|  The leaf touches no sessckpt/matjournal source: live `git status` shows\n24|  exactly `M LOGBOOK.md README.md` + 4 traceability files and\n25|  `?? internal/crashgate/`.\n26|- Live worktree == candidate tree: the 6 tracked files show zero diff\n27|  against `25b762c`, and `diff -r` of `internal/crashgate/` against\n28|  `git archive 25b762c` is byte-identical.\n29|- `task-board.config.json` byte-identical to trunk (`cmp` clean).\n30|- Hygiene: no `__pycache__`/`.pyc` under crashgate/sessckpt/matjournal;\n31|  `gofmt -l internal` empty; `go vet` clean on all four packages (exit 0);\n32|  `cataloggen -adopted -output internal/catalog/catalog_gen.go -check`\n33|  exit 0 after `go generate ./...` with no worktree side effects.\n34|\n35|## 2. Registry derivation — PASS\n36|\n37|- Independent probe (module-internal, git-ignored scratch, since removed)\n38|  re-parsed Section 13.13 with its own range scanner: parsed=94\n39|  (12 table ranges + 1 prose range), registered=94, missing=[], extra=[].\n40|- Renamed-ID sensitivity proved in the isolated copy: `CR-MAT-01` →\n41|  `CR-MAT-0X` makes `TestRegistryDerivesFromPinnedSpec` FAIL with\n42|  `missing [\"CR-MAT-01\"], extra [\"CR-MAT-0X\"]` (exit 1).\n43|- N/A audit by script: 48 reachable paths / 31 IDs, 121 N/A paths /\n44|  63 IDs — exactly the claimed counts — and NO checkpoint/journal-class\n45|  boundary is left without a driver.\n46|- 10 N/A spot-checks against the landed code: no `clone`/`sync`/`bridge`/\n47|  `lifecycle` packages exist; `terminalbackend` has no creation runtime\n48|  (manifest/probe/conformance only); `provider` has no process-start or\n49|  persistence runtime; `localstore`/`sessrepo`-adjacent rows are\n50|  `WriteExternal` with disclosed out-of-story-boundary notes; no `doctor`\n51|  surface exists. No row whose durable fact is a checkpoint capture or\n52|  journal transition is marked N/A.\n53|\n54|## 3. Conformance records — PASS, plus 5 independent reviewer probes\n55|\n56|- Producer tarball holds 74 `conformance/*.json` records; all 74 validate\n57|  mechanically (required fields present, `selected` in the 3-outcome enum,\n58|  boundary ID in the registry).\n59|- Live reruns (exit 0): full `crashgate` package, `TestRealSIGKILLSeams`\n60|  twice (checkpoint_capture + journal_create), `TestCrashGateRejections`,\n61|  `TestCrashGateMutualExclusion`, `TestCrashGateSection1312` (8 subtests).\n62|- Reviewer probes (`reviewer_probe_test.go` in the evidence tarball, run\n63|  in the isolated copy, 5/5 PASS, log attached):\n64|  - CR-STOP-02 own AfterBlob crash → identical retry converges\n65|    byte-identical, one checkpoint identity (safe_retry semantics).\n66|  - CR-STOP-02 torn variant (disagreeing bytes at the digest path) →\n67|    retry refuses `ErrCheckpointConflict`, torn bytes preserved, nothing\n68|    installed.\n69|  - CR-MAT-03 torn variant (truncated `journal.json`) → exactly\n70|    `recoverable_parked_state` with durable `recovery.json`, frozen phase.\n71|  - CR-MAT-06-path adopt crash + substituted native handle → exactly\n72|    `recoverable_parked_state`, fail-closed, manager reference unchanged.\n73|  - Rollback-facts + moved-lease ordering attack → exactly\n74|    `recoverable_parked_state`, rollback NOT executed (phase stays\n75|    staging, blocking `last_error` recorded).\n76|- Two initial probe expectations were corrected during the run (both were\n77|  probe errors, not product findings, reasoning recorded here): a torn\n78|  journal cannot name operation IDs (quarantine evidence by construction),\n79|  and the native-substitution gate applies only where a bound identity\n80|  exists (`nativeRequired`: committed provider or adopted/resumed bridge),\n81|  so substitution at the opened-but-unadopted stage is correctly out of\n82|  that gate's scope — the harness proves substitution rejection where the\n83|  gate applies (adopted binding).\n84|\n85|## 4. Exclusivity and rejections — PASS\n86|\n87|- `grep` over crashgate + matjournal sources and records: the only outcome\n88|  strings are `safe_retry`, `explicit_rollback`, `recoverable_parked_state`\n89|  (the constant definitions). No fourth outcome exists.\n90|- The 10 shipped rejection rows pass live; the reviewer ordering attack\n91|  above proves conflicting rollback/parked evidence parks without\n92|  executing rollback.\n93|\n94|## 5. Section 13.12 — PASS (7 of 19 driven, 8 subtests green)\n95|\n96|- The 12 unlanded-owner rows verified against the tree (sync flow, lease\n97|  arbitration, provider runtime/adapter, bridge, lifecycle orchestration,\n98|  clone flow absent or partial-landed as claimed).\n99|\n100|## 6. Mutation — PASS\n101|\n102|- Producer harness reproduced in the isolated copy: 9 KILLED + 1 control\n103|  SURVIVED, 0 not-applied, 0 anomalies (summary + per-plant logs in\n104|  evidence). `N-registry-grace11` shows static pass + behavior fail,\n105|  proving the token-preserving mutant runs the behavioral suite.\n106|- Each of the 9 KILLED re-run twice more (named killer only): all exits\n107|  `[1, 1]`, zero rerun failures.\n108|- 4 reviewer-owned narrowing mutants on predicates the producer did not\n109|  mutate (isolated copy, logs in evidence): `R-lease-forward`,\n110|  `R-substitution-leaseactive`, `R-exhaustiveness-rollback-contradiction`,\n111|  `R-registry-stop02` (static pass + behavior fail — second\n112|  token-preserving proof) — all KILLED; `R-control-comment` SURVIVED.\n113|\n114|## 7. Story-close items — PASS\n115|\n116|- `section:13.13` partial 9/11 with the `#4`/`#5` journal-halves gap\n117|  disclosed; `section:13.12` stays `unmeasured`, which is the honest and\n118|  gate-required level (the scanner cannot measure table-shaped sections;\n119|  claiming `partial` would be refused; the gap names the 7 driven rows and\n120|  the harness case). 2 new acceptance cases present;\n(more lines below)","final_result":true}}}
