ilt `/tmp/republish_resolutions.json` (header copied from the retained\n24|   `resolution-template.json`: branch `bde093e…`, trunk `9e9fe51…`,\n25|   candidate tree `25b762c…`) with resolution #1:\n26|   `{checkpoint_oid: 8a757e0…, path: LOGBOOK.md,\n27|   sha256: c30af45c4e5999920404b30f0bd484c8e3659fbdeb63113fb12f72887341c508}`\n28|   (trunk entries `3uzfyn`, `kp4zpu` first, then the checkpoint's `14yo67`\n29|   entry, newest-first; everything else byte-identical).\n30|3. Re-ran with `--replay-resolutions` → checkpoint 1 replayed; stopped at\n31|   checkpoint `bde093e242b688d8348818706e4720fed3eec96d` with six\n32|   conflicted files (retained replay `replay-1380464330`). The trunk side\n33|   and the checkpoint side both extended the traceability registry and\n34|   figures, so a LOGBOOK-only resolution was insufficient; each file got a\n35|   union resolution:\n36|   - `LOGBOOK.md` (sha256 `64ccbe9dcb4a…`): trunk entries + `3k3e6m` entry.\n37|   - `README.md` (`4682b10c08d5…`): replay-merged figures (117 cases,\n38|     59 bindings) + trunk prose.\n39|   - `internal/traceability/ownership.v0.6.0.json` (`c6c7df42277a…`):\n40|     case union 101 shared + 12 trunk + 4 checkpoint = 117; ownership\n41|     arrays were already identical on both sides.\n42|   - `internal/traceability/traceability.go` (`afb6e8e00725…`): digest\n43|     re-pinned to the merged projection\n44|     `89e9e8fd1a42363673be341e0600a6dff0085cfd143705d946f901272977eef0`\n45|     (read from the `tracecheck` refusal line, then verified green).\n46|   - `internal/traceability/traceability_test.go` (`619d217ec855…`) and\n47|     `cmd/tracecheck/main_test.go` (`5b535c3630b0…`): pins set to the\n48|     merged report (`bindings=59 full=2 partial=4 sliver=3 unevidenced=46\n49|     unmeasured=4 unowned=12 clauses_discharged=29/489`).\n50|   Merged-report truth was established by running the real `tracecheck`\n51|   and `go test ./internal/traceability/...` inside the replay worktree\n52|   (both green) before sealing the resolutions.\n53|4. Re-ran with the 7-resolution file → `refresh_advanced`, new branch tip\n54|   `813b05d3c43605c8e54a8d54f410455b6463b086`.\n55|5. Verified: parent chain `813b05d → 8299fdc → 9e9fe51`; both replayed\n56|   commits signed (`git verify-commit` OK); `git diff 9e9fe51 8299fdc`\n57|   shows only the 14yo67 delta (10 files), `git diff 8299fdc 813b05d`\n58|   only the 3k3e6m delta (19 files). Note: the republish brief expected\n59|   `git diff <original> <replayed>` to be empty except LOGBOOK.md; that\n60|   holds only for LOGBOOK-single-conflict refreshes. Here trunk changed\n61|   the same traceability files, so the replayed trees necessarily carry\n62|   the merged figures — the per-delta check above is the meaningful\n63|   invariant and it holds.\n64|\n65|## Stale-copy audit (path-by-path)\n66|\n67|After the refresh the working tree overlaid pre-refresh bytes on the new\n68|HEAD. 59 non-candidate paths restored verbatim with\n69|`git checkout HEAD -- <path>` (list in `/tmp/republish_restore_list.txt`\n70|during the run; classes below):\n71|\n72|| Class | Paths | Action |\n73|| --- | --- | --- |\n74|| `.task-board/` activity/progress (checkout artifact) | 10 M/D entries | restored to HEAD |\n75|| Trunk-landed packages (`internal/provhost`, `internal/resumesmoke`, `internal/sessprofile`, `internal/environ`, `internal/secprim`) | 49 M/D entries | restored to HEAD |\n76|| `task-board.config.json` | unmodified | equals HEAD byte-for-byte (`cmp` clean); no Story-carried delta |\n77|\n78|The six candidate paths were hand-merged (HEAD content + rev1 candidate\n79|delta re-applied; never wholesale checkout):\n80|\n81|| Candidate path | Merge |\n82|| --- | --- |\n83|| `LOGBOOK.md` | rev1 17ootk entry re-prepended onto HEAD (figures refreshed: 119 cases, digest `ba242a9d…0937afd`) + 3-line REPUBLISH bullet; diff vs HEAD purely additive |\n84|| `README.md` | crashgate package section re-inserted at the matjournal anchor (byte-identical block);